  "body": "  In Python a module is:      A file containing Python definitions and statements intended for use in other Python programs.   A module can be reused in different programs.     A separate block of code within a program.   While a module is separate block of code, it is separate from a program.     One line of code in a program.   The call to a feature within a module may be one line of code, but modules are usually multiple lines of code separate from the program     A file that contains documentation about functions in Python.   Each module has its own documentation, but the module itself is more than just documentation.    "
