  "body": "  Suppose you are going to write a recusive function to calculate the factorial of a number. fact(n) returns n * n-1 * n-2 * … * 1, and the factorial of zero is definded to be 1. What would be the most appropriate base case?      n == 0    Although this would work there are better and slightly more efficient choices. since fact(1) and fact(0) are the same.      n == 1    A good choice, but what happens if you call fact(0)?      n >= 0    This basecase would be true for all numbers greater than zero so fact of any positive number would be 1.      n <= 1    Good, this is the most efficient, and even keeps your program from crashing if you try to compute the factorial of a negative number.     "
