  "body": "  Rewrite the following 3 lines of code with a single assert:  result = engage_thruster(22) if result != 'OK': print(\"Test 2: FAIL\")      assert result != 'OK'   Incorrect. The assert should call the engage_thruster function. Try again.     assert engage_thruster(22) == result   Incorrect. The assert should not assume the presence of a variable named result.     assert engage_thruster(22) != 'OK'   Incorrect. This assert calls the engage_thruster function with the correct parameter, but interprets the result differently from the if statement provided.     assert engage_thruster(22) == 'OK'   Correct! This assert checks that the result of invoking engage_thruster(22) is the value 'OK'.    "
