  "id": "mc_testable_2",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "unit-testing_designing-testable-functions.html#mc_testable_2",
  "type": "Checkpoint",
  "number": "20.4.3",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Consider the following function. What would an appropriate precondition be?   def getfirst(msg): \"\"\"returns first character of msg\"\"\" return msg[0]       len(msg) <= 0   Incorrect. The function would crash if this condition were true.     len(msg) > 0   Correct. The function cannot return the first character of an empty msg.     msg == \"\"   Incorrect. The function would crash if this condition were true.     none of these   Incorrect. Try again.    "
